<section aria-labelledby="appendix-murmurhash3" class="post-section l-page hash-case">
<span aria-hidden="true" class="section-anchor" id="murmur"></span>
<h3 class="l-body" id="appendix-murmurhash3" data-toc-label="MurmurHash3 x64_128">MurmurHash3 x64_128 <span class="pattern-tags"><span class="pattern-label">pattern:</span> <a href="#pattern-p2" title="public arithmetic">P2</a> · <a href="#pattern-p6" title="collision generators">P6</a> · <a href="#pattern-p7" title="top bits and carries">P7</a></span></h3>
<p class="l-body reader-summary">The attacker introduces a controlled difference early in the hash and cancels it with later message data. The construction works without knowing the seed and makes both halves of the output agree.</p>
